# Intro

Idealised cluster made of gas and stars. A black hole lies at the center of the cluster.

# Configure

To run this example with the EAGLE model, SWIFT must be configured with the following options:

./configure --with-subgrid=EAGLE

To run this example with the GEAR model, configure SWIFT with:

./configure --with-subgrid=GEAR-BH --with-grackle=$GRACKLE_ROOT

# Run

To run with EAGLE, type:

with_subgrid=EAGLE run.sh

To run with GEAR, your first must change the parameter file:

```
  particle_splitting:            0    # Particle splitting is ON
  recording_triggers_part: [-1, -1]   # Not recording as we have many snapshots
  recording_triggers_bpart: [-1, -1]  # Not recording as we have many snapshots 
```

to

```
  particle_splitting:                1    # Particle splitting is OFF. GEAR does not have splitting.
  recording_triggers_part: [-1, -1, -1]   # Not recording as we have many snapshots
  recording_triggers_bpart: [-1, -1, -1]  # Not recording as we have many snapshots
  recording_triggers_sink: [-1, -1, -1]   # Not recording as we have many snapshots
```
  
with_subgrid=GEAR run.sh

